# Conventional Commits

Always write git commit messages in [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) form:

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short description>

<optional body>
```

## Types

Use one of: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

## Rules

- Subject line: imperative mood, lowercase after the type, no trailing period, ~72 chars or less
- Prefer a scope when it clarifies the area (`feat(hooks):`, `fix(claims):`)
- Body (optional) explains **why**, not a file list
- Breaking changes: add `!` after type/scope (`feat(api)!: ...`) and/or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Never use unstructured subjects like "Harden X" or "Update stuff" — pick a type first

## Examples

```
feat(claims): refuse release of another seat's live claim

fix(repo): key PM and claims on stable repo_id

test: add smoke coverage for PM auto-CC and claims

chore: extract agent-bus into its own repo
```
